# Packages come from the approved Microsoft proxy, never the public registry.
#
# Committed rather than left to a developer's ~/.npmrc: a user-level setting
# does not travel with the checkout, is invisible to CI and to a fresh clone,
# and cannot be reviewed. This file is the one place the feed is stated, and it
# is stated in the repository so every environment reads the same answer.
#
# No credential belongs here. This records a package source, which is build
# configuration and is published the same way the Python feed is in
# pyproject.toml, the Dockerfile and docs/azure-prerequisites.md. A token would
# be a secret and must stay in the user-level file or the environment.
#
# Note that this setting alone is not sufficient. It governs where npm *looks
# up* a package; once package-lock.json exists, installs fetch the literal URL
# in each entry's `resolved` field. Both have to agree, and
# test_packages_come_from_the_approved_feed.py holds them together.
registry=https://packagefeedproxy.microsoft.io/npm/
